===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|salz|lang=goh}} (akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|salt|lang=osx}}, Old Dutch ''salt'', Old English {{term|sealt|lang=ang}}, Old Norse {{term|salt|lang=non}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|saltan|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|seh₂l-|séh₂l-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|séh₂ls|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Dutch {{term|zout|lang=nl}}, English {{term|salt|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|salt|lang=da}}.

